---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base title="About" description="What MastersVault is and how it's made.">
  <div class="container page prose">
    <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is a free, open-source practice site for graduate admissions tests. It offers full-length mock
      tests, shorter section practice and revision notes, all delivered on a test screen that works like the real
      exam's. That way, the timer, the navigation rules and the question formats won't surprise you on test day.
    </p>

    <h2>Original questions</h2>
    <p>
      Every question on this site is written for {SITE.name}. We don't copy, adapt or paraphrase questions from
      official guides, official practice tests or other prep providers. Each question is checked for a single
      defensible answer and comes with a full explanation.
    </p>

    <h2>Found a mistake?</h2>
    <p>
      Every question has a "Report an issue" link that opens a pre-filled issue on <a href={SITE.repo}>GitHub</a>.
      Corrections are very welcome.
    </p>

    <h2>Licences</h2>
    <p>
      © 2026 the {SITE.name} contributors. The questions, passages, explanations and notes are licensed under <a
        href={SITE.contentLicense.url}>{SITE.contentLicense.name}</a
      >: you may share and adapt them for non-commercial purposes, with credit, under the same licence. The site's
      code is licensed under <a href={SITE.codeLicense.url}>{SITE.codeLicense.name}</a>, and its source is on <a
        href={SITE.repo}>GitHub</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is built with open-source software, including Astro, React and KaTeX, and is set in IBM Plex Mono.
      Their copyright notices and licences are in the <a href={url('/licenses.txt')}>third-party licences</a> file.
    </p>

    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is independent and has no connection to any test maker. See the <a href={url('/disclaimer/')}
        >disclaimer</a
      > for details.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
